   {
    "day": 51,
    "text": "With Haven grieving, Stonebridge installs their own speaker at the table. Tribute rises to 11,250 kcal/week. Grief is leverage, and they know it. The link holds — it was never with one person."
   },
   {
    "day": 51,
    "text": "🕯️ Christopher Álvarez is dead — combat. The village stops. Somebody screams. Somebody else starts digging."
   },
   {
    "day": 51,
    "text": "The Codex doesn't pause for grief. Aurora blinks — and it's already there, overlaying everything, syncing. No pen. No paper. The mantle just... transfers."
   },
   {
    "day": 51,
    "text": "📖 The Codex turns a page on its own. Marcus is dead. You didn't ask. It knew."
   },
   {
    "day": 51,
    "text": "The table is being set — a lesser seat, priced for what you built. They are watching to see who comes to it."
